/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tridione","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Tridione; Troxidone; Trimetin","reason":"Adds NCBI MeSH entry terms for the same drug.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not describe QT effect.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"N/A - FDA label does not describe a QT interval effect.","reason":"FDA label exists but does not mention QT.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was retained in the PubMed RCT audit/gap review as of 05-19-2026; RCT section set to N/A per current scope.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was located in PubMed for trimethadione/Tridione/Troxidone/Trimetin as of 05-21-2026; RCT/outcome fields remain N/A.","reason":"Updates alias coverage and audit date.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=%28trimethadione+OR+Tridione+OR+Troxidone+OR+Trimetin%29+%28placebo+OR+randomized+OR+double-blind%29+epilepsy","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293"]},{"current_value":"N/A - no current FDA/DailyMed label located and FDA Orange Book product listing does not provide dosing.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"3 or 4 divided doses daily.","reason":"FDA label provides dosing frequency.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","pmid":"","proposed_action":"Keep N/A; no existing PubMed RCT links were provided and no qualifying trimethadione phase II/III placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT was found.","rationale":"Searches for trimethadione and MeSH aliases returned historical non-RCT treatment reports or unrelated drug trials, not a qualifying placebo-controlled trimethadione RCT.","status":"verified","url":"N/A"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA accessdata/Drugs@FDA Tridione (trimethadione) label; NCBI MeSH/PubMed search audit; Epilepsy Foundation availability note.","reason":"DailyMed should not be used for black-box verification, and the FDA accessdata label supports many row facts currently marked unavailable.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/orange-book-data-files","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68014293","https://www.epilepsy.com/stories/community-corner-new-drug-alerts"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed search on 05-20-2026: no current label found for terms [trimethadione; Tridione].","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata Tridione (trimethadione) label, NDA 005856/S-021, approved 06-06-2012; top warning/boxed warning verified 05-21-2026.","reason":"FDA label was found; DailyMed is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2012/005856s021ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata Tridione label (Description/Clinical Pharmacology)","reason":"Orange Book does not support the mechanism/pharmacology wording; FDA label does.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2012/005856s021lbl.pdf"]}],"summary":"Needs update. The major issue is that the row repeatedly says no FDA label was located, but an FDA accessdata Tridione label and approval letter exist. That label supports a top warning, refractory petit mal/absence indication, adverse-reaction list without percentages, liver microsomal metabolism, and adult/pediatric divided dosing. RCT/outcome N/A values remain appropriate because no qualifying placebo-controlled phase II/III trimethadione epilepsy RCT was found."}
